#!/bin/sh
# Pushing to master triggers the deploy workflow, which builds from the
# PROFILE_TS_B64 secret rather than from the working tree. If profile.ts has
# been edited since the secret was last uploaded, that deploy silently ships
# the previous content. Sync first.
#
# Enable once per clone:  git config core.hooksPath .githooks
# Bypass in a pinch:      git push --no-verify

while read -r _local_ref _local_sha remote_ref _remote_sha; do
  case "$remote_ref" in
    refs/heads/master) ;;
    *) continue ;;
  esac

  if [ ! -f src/data/profile.ts ]; then
    echo "pre-push: src/data/profile.ts not present — skipping secret sync." >&2
    exit 0
  fi

  if ! command -v gh >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "pre-push: gh not found — cannot verify PROFILE_TS_B64 is current." >&2
    echo "          Install the GitHub CLI or push with --no-verify." >&2
    exit 1
  fi

  if ! node scripts/sync-profile-secret.mjs; then
    echo "pre-push: secret sync failed — the deploy would ship stale content." >&2
    exit 1
  fi

  exit 0
done

exit 0
